  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 2.359999895095825,
      "text": "Begin with the selected pollen section.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 3.119999885559082,
      "end": 6.960000038146973,
      "text": "A marks the outer exine and B the inner intine.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 6.960000038146973,
      "end": 10.640000343322754,
      "text": "C points to a germ pore region where the exine is interrupted.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 11.380000114440918,
      "end": 15.84000015258789,
      "text": "The resistant exine contains sporopollenin, while intine is mainly cellulose",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 15.84000015258789,
      "end": 16.399999618530273,
      "text": "and pectin.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 17.139999389648438,
      "end": 20.940000534057617,
      "text": "The opening in exine is not an empty hole through every layer of the living",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 20.940000534057617,
      "end": 21.459999084472656,
      "text": "pollen grain.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 22.239999771118164,
      "end": 25.3799991607666,
      "text": "During germination, the developing tube emerges through an aperture.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 26.15999984741211,
      "end": 30.280000686645508,
      "text": "Only one germ pore region is selected here; pollen grains vary in aperture",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 30.280000686645508,
      "end": 32.220001220703125,
      "text": "number, shape and surface pattern.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 32.959999084472656,
      "end": 37.31999969482422,
      "text": "This smooth teaching outline is therefore not a species diagnosis or a",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 37.31999969482422,
      "end": 38.02000045776367,
      "text": "measurement of wall thickness.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 38.616000000000575,
      "end": 42.45599991416989,
      "text": "D labels the vegetative nucleus within the large vegetative cell.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 43.59600001907406,
      "end": 47.956000152588466,
      "text": "E labels the smaller generative cell, with its own nucleus represented inside.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 48.616000000000575,
      "end": 52.99600011444149,
      "text": "The boundary around E is a cell boundary; the oval at D is a nucleus.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 53.87600022888241,
      "end": 56.952666131631496,
      "text": "Counting every circle as a separate cell would therefore give the wrong",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 56.952666131631496,
      "end": 57.25599938964901,
      "text": "answer.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 57.97600061035214,
      "end": 60.55600053405819,
      "text": "This board illustrates a two celled pollen stage.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 61.41599923706112,
      "end": 64.97600061035214,
      "text": "Some species shed pollen at this stage, while others shed it after the",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 64.97600061035214,
      "end": 66.39600068664609,
      "text": "generative cell has already divided.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 66.95600015258847,
      "end": 70.71599847412168,
      "text": "The pollen grain is the male gametophyte, not simply one sperm cell.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 71.75599938964902,
      "end": 75.37599832153379,
      "text": "Distinguish the whole gametophyte, its cells and the nuclei within those cells",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 75.83600122070371,
      "end": 76.71599847412168,
      "text": "before applying a count.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 76.87200000000114,
      "end": 79.35200001907462,
      "text": "The second board compares selected stages.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 80.23199989509696,
      "end": 83.49199988556022,
      "text": "A contains one vegetative nucleus and a generative cell.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 84.172000190736,
      "end": 88.59302568699877,
      "text": "The arrow represents mitosis of the generative cell, producing two haploid",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 88.59302568699877,
      "end": 88.83200003814811,
      "text": "male",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 88.83200003814811,
      "end": 89.13200022888297,
      "text": "gametes.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 89.83200003814811,
      "end": 93.41323380449197,
      "text": "This is not the earlier meiosis of a diploid microspore mother cell in the",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 93.41323380449197,
      "end": 93.75199916076774,
      "text": "anther.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 94.77199961853141,
      "end": 97.35199954223746,
      "text": "B shows a germinating example after that division.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 98.05200030517692,
      "end": 101.95584594550613,
      "text": "The small circles in its tube represent the male gametes, while the oval is",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 101.95584594550613,
      "end": 102.1119997711193,
      "text": "the",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 102.1119997711193,
      "end": 102.97200038147086,
      "text": "vegetative nucleus.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 103.55200030517692,
      "end": 107.13200022888297,
      "text": "Their relative positions are illustrative rather than a universal migration",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 107.13200022888297,
      "end": 107.43199946594352,
      "text": "order.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 108.39200045776481,
      "end": 112.22917851687814,
      "text": "If pollen is shed at the three celled stage, the two male gametes already",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 112.22917851687814,
      "end": 112.4919989318859,
      "text": "exist",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 112.4919989318859,
      "end": 113.39200045776481,
      "text": "before germination.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 114.13199832153434,
      "end": 117.29199816894645,
      "text": "Do not make one developmental timetable a rule for every species.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 117.8880000000018,
      "end": 121.44799994278134,
      "text": "At B, the pollen tube emerges through a gap in exine.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 122.22800015258969,
      "end": 126.02800034332455,
      "text": "It is an outgrowth of the vegetative cell and provides a route for delivery of",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 126.02800034332455,
      "end": 126.92799996185482,
      "text": "the male gametes.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 127.6080002670306,
      "end": 131.6080002670306,
      "text": "On a receptive stigma, successful growth depends on the pollen pistil",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 131.6080002670306,
      "end": 135.0080008392352,
      "text": "interaction, not merely on a grain landing anywhere.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 135.90800045776547,
      "end": 140.06800030517758,
      "text": "Pollination is the transfer of pollen to the stigma; fertilisation is a later",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 140.06800030517758,
      "end": 140.7679991607684,
      "text": "fusion event.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 141.68799923706234,
      "end": 145.58800076294125,
      "text": "Pollen can also germinate in suitable laboratory medium, but laboratory",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 145.58800076294125,
      "end": 149.58800076294125,
      "text": "germination alone does not prove that a particular pistil will accept it.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 150.20799969482601,
      "end": 154.46800183105648,
      "text": "The drawing does not provide a culture recipe, growth rate measurement or",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 154.46800183105648,
      "end": 156.3880000000018,
      "text": "evidence that every tube reaches an ovule.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 156.60000000000238,
      "end": 158.8200000286126,
      "text": "The pistil section locates the pathway.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 159.69999990463495,
      "end": 165.49999961853266,
      "text": "A labels the stigma, B the style, C the ovary and D a selected ovule.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 166.4199996948266,
      "end": 170.3623077539321,
      "text": "Follow the paired path from a pollen grain on the stigma, through the style",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 170.3623077539321,
      "end": 170.52000007629633,
      "text": "and",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 170.52000007629633,
      "end": 171.24000034332514,
      "text": "into the ovary.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 171.83999977112055,
      "end": 176.04000053406,
      "text": "The path represents one compatible pollen tube, not a claim that a pistil",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 176.04000053406,
      "end": 179.05999908447504,
      "text": "accepts only one grain or grows only one tube.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 179.46000061035394,
      "end": 183.55999908447504,
      "text": "The tube does not become the style, and it is not a xylem vessel carrying",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 183.55999908447504,
      "end": 183.94000015259027,
      "text": "water.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 183.94000015259027,
      "end": 186.7599998474145,
      "text": "Different tissues guide and support its growth.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 187.47999916076898,
      "end": 191.94000015259027,
      "text": "The diagram omits other ovules and many cellular details so that the route",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 191.94000015259027,
      "end": 193.1600013732934,
      "text": "remains easy to trace.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 193.4640000000029,
      "end": 197.58399988556198,
      "text": "At the bottom of the selected ovule, the path bends toward the micropylar",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 197.58399988556198,
      "end": 197.9839999809294,
      "text": "opening.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 198.74400020981125,
      "end": 202.44399954223923,
      "text": "In the common route illustrated here, the pollen tube enters through the",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 202.44399954223923,
      "end": 204.78399969482712,
      "text": "micropyle and then reaches a synergid.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 205.48400045776657,
      "end": 209.123999847415,
      "text": "Do not confuse the micropyle with the hilum, which is the attachment junction",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 209.123999847415,
      "end": 210.92399908447555,
      "text": "discussed in the previous class.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 211.8040001525908,
      "end": 215.38400007629684,
      "text": "Nor should the tube be drawn through the egg before it reaches the embryo sac.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 216.123999847415,
      "end": 220.3040001525908,
      "text": "Other routes of ovule entry occur in some plants, so the selected common",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 220.3040001525908,
      "end": 222.26399923706344,
      "text": "pathway is not a universal claim.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 223.16400076294235,
      "end": 226.84400106811813,
      "text": "Section orientation can turn this route upside down on a page; structure",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 226.84400106811813,
      "end": 229.44399954223923,
      "text": "relationships matter more than whether the arrow points down.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 229.6800000000034,
      "end": 232.62000005722385,
      "text": "The final board enlarges the micropylar region.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 233.3800000476871,
      "end": 237.23999994278293,
      "text": "The tube enters the left synergid through the represented filiform apparatus.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 238.15999954223972,
      "end": 241.0600001144443,
      "text": "Two male gametes are shown released into that synergid.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 241.65999954223972,
      "end": 245.73999946594577,
      "text": "The central egg is separate, and the right synergid is not a second egg.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 246.4600006866489,
      "end": 250.37282003549768,
      "text": "The filiform apparatus is a specialised wall structure associated with",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 250.37282003549768,
      "end": 250.81999938965183,
      "text": "synergid",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 250.81999938965183,
      "end": 252.81999938965183,
      "text": "function and pollen tube guidance.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 253.22000091553073,
      "end": 257.2599999237094,
      "text": "It is not a bundle of flagella used by sperm to swim through the style.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 257.7800003814731,
      "end": 261.70000045776703,
      "text": "The drawing omits most of the embryo sac boundary and the integuments.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 262.83999984741547,
      "end": 266.83999984741547,
      "text": "Treat the destination arrows as a conceptual summary rather than a measured",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 266.83999984741547,
      "end": 268.33999984741547,
      "text": "movie of gamete movement.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 268.728000000004,
      "end": 270.5480000524561,
      "text": "Follow the two destination arrows.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 271.228000000004,
      "end": 275.23056413680257,
      "text": "One male gamete fuses with the haploid egg to form the diploid zygote:",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 275.23056413680257,
      "end": 275.68800003815096,
      "text": "syngamy.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 276.50800020981234,
      "end": 280.64800007629793,
      "text": "The other fuses with the central cell nuclear complement, represented here by",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 280.64800007629793,
      "end": 285.3480008392374,
      "text": "two haploid polar nuclei, producing the triploid primary endosperm nucleus.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 285.92800076294344,
      "end": 287.8480008392374,
      "text": "That second event is triple fusion.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 288.4880002288858,
      "end": 292.0080006866495,
      "text": "The vegetative nucleus is not one of those three participating nuclei.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 292.8679993896524,
      "end": 296.68799908447664,
      "text": "Syngamy and triple fusion together constitute double fertilisation in the",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 296.68799908447664,
      "end": 298.1079991607706,
      "text": "typical angiosperm model.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 298.74800045776766,
      "end": 302.50799877930086,
      "text": "The embryo develops from the zygote, whereas endosperm develops through the",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 302.50799877930086,
      "end": 303.18799908447664,
      "text": "other pathway.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 303.8080018310587,
      "end": 307.9480012207071,
      "text": "The board summarises these destinations; it does not already depict a mature",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 307.9480012207071,
      "end": 311.1840000000047,
      "text": "seed or every possible endosperm ploidy.",
      "chapter": 7
    }
  ]
}
